# HyperBabel React Native Demo — Environment Variables
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and edit only what you need.
# .env.local is gitignored so your local overrides never leak.

# ── HyperBabel API endpoint ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Points at production by default — that is the right value for almost every
# integrator. Override only if you operate HyperBabel on a private domain.
EXPO_PUBLIC_HB_API_URL=https://api.hyperbabel.com/api/v1

# ── Firebase ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# There are NO Firebase-related environment variables in this demo. The
# native Firebase SDK reads everything from the two config files you drop
# into firebase/ (see firebase/README.md). All Customer Auth runs through
# pattern B1 — Firebase Direct Exchange:
#
#   1. Sign in with Firebase on device     → Firebase ID token
#   2. POST /customer/auth/firebase-exchange  → HyperBabel customer JWT
#   3. SecureStore the JWT pair, attach to every subsequent API call
#
# Your HyperBabel org API key never ships in the binary. The demo throws
# at startup if it sees one.
